spec:
  grid: 21-25 rows x 21-26 cols, bg=0
  frame:
    color: 8 [observed]
    shape: 7-10 rows x 6-9 cols rectangle, only 4 corner L-pieces present (no straight edges)
    structure: |
      Each corner is a 2x2 L (3 cells). 3 corners use frame_color (9 cells total),
      1 corner uses fill_color (3 cells). All 4 corners occupied, no empty corner.
      Interior is pure bg. Example (F=frame, L=fill, .=bg):
        F F . . . L L
        F . . . . . L
        . . . . . . .
        F . . . . . F
        F F . . . F F
    fill_corner: varies across TL/TR/BL/BR (one per example)
    margin_to_edge: >=4 on all sides
  fill_color: non-bg, non-frame color; used to flood the cross in output
  markers:
    description: single pixels of various colors scattered across the grid
    arm_markers: 6-14 total, placed in the cross region (same rows or cols as frame) but outside the frame rect
    per_arm: >=1 marker per arm (top/bottom/left/right)
    stacking: 0-1 pairs of markers may share a column (top/bottom) or row (left/right) in an arm
    outside_markers: 3-12 pixels scattered in the 4 quadrants outside the cross; unchanged in output
    colors: 6-7 distinct marker colors (excluding bg, frame, fill); each marker is 1 pixel
  output_transform: |
    1. Fill the cross (union of frame rows and frame cols, full grid width/height) with fill_color where bg.
    2. For each arm marker, cast a ray outward from frame: top markers ray upward, bottom downward,
       left leftward, right rightward. Ray paints marker color from marker to grid edge, stopping
       at the next marker in the same line. Markers closer to frame are painted over by markers farther.
    3. Redraw the complete rectangular frame border with frame_color (all 4 sides solid).
    4. Frame interior filled with fill_color. Pixels outside the cross are unchanged.
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Pick grid size (21-25 x 21-26), frame size (7-10 x 6-9), and place frame with >=4 margin on all sides.
    - Choose fill_corner (TL/TR/BL/BR). Build the output cross filled with fill_color, solid frame border.
    - Place arm markers in the cross arms. For each arm, pick 1-5 markers at distinct row/col positions
      (allow at most 1 shared col/row pair per arm). Each marker has a unique color from a pool of 6-7 colors.
    - Compute rays outward from each marker to grid edge or next marker. Paint rays in output.
    - Scatter 3-12 single-pixel markers of various colors in the 4 quadrants outside the cross.
    - Derive input by undoing the transform. Remove all fill from the cross (set to bg). Remove rays
      (set to bg), keeping only the original marker pixels. Replace the solid frame border with the
      3-corner-L + 1-fill-L skeleton (12 cells total). Keep outside markers as-is.
